What:		/sys/class/hidg/hidg<N>/pending_ms
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	7.3
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) How long, in milliseconds, the report at the controller
		has waited for the host to read it from the interrupt IN
		endpoint, or 0 when no report is waiting. It stays near the
		endpoint's polling interval while the host reads, and grows
		while the host does not: busy, suspended, or without a driver
		for the interface. With the function's keep_latest option a
		write never waits for the host, so this is how userspace can
		tell that the host stopped reading.
